<%--
Callout - inline alert banner: icon + title / body / actions

$variant - "danger" | "warning" (required; the component throws otherwise)
$icon - leading icon class string, e.g. "bi bi-exclamation-triangle" [optional]

<Slot:title> - the bold headline (required)
<Slot:body> - the explanation line [optional]
<Slot:actions> - trailing action buttons [optional]

The one inline-alert shape (an overdue-invoice warning, a soft-deleted-record
banner). Rendered as a Bootstrap .alert, so padding, radius and border arrive through the
theme-aware --bs-alert-* set. The surface is deliberately re-pointed at the
neutral tertiary background: a colored left accent + colored icon/title carry the
variant, and the body reads calm (serious-tool restraint, not a tinted Bootstrap
alert). Variant is validated loudly - a typo fails, never renders unstyled.

Usage:
    <Callout $variant="warning" $icon="bi bi-exclamation-triangle">
        <Slot:title>This invoice is overdue</Slot:title>
        <Slot:body>The balance was due on Jun 30, 2026.</Slot:body>
    </Callout>
--%>
<Define:Callout tag="div" class="alert">
    <% if (this.args.variant !== 'danger' && this.args.variant !== 'warning') { %>
        <% throw new Error('Callout requires $variant "danger" or "warning"'); %>
    <% } %>
    <% if (this.args.icon) { %>
        <i class="Callout__icon <%= this.args.icon %>"></i>
    <% } %>
    <div class="Callout__content">
        <div class="Callout__title"><%= content('title') %></div>
        <% if (this.args._slots && this.args._slots.body) { %>
            <div class="Callout__body"><%= content('body') %></div>
        <% } %>
    </div>
    <% if (this.args._slots && this.args._slots.actions) { %>
        <div class="Callout__actions"><%= content('actions') %></div>
    <% } %>
</Define:Callout>
